{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For there is no truth in their mouth</b> — In the mouth of each one of them, as in: 'she refused to be comforted … for he is not' (Jeremiah 31:15). And 'truth' is an adjective for 'word,' or [read] דברה and thus [it] means 'answers brazenly, and his food is fat.'" "<b>Their throat</b> — It is the hidden heart." "<b>Destruction</b> — From the root הוה. It is an imperative: 'contrive for the king,' that they think evil thoughts — perhaps they will be and arise." "<b>An open grave</b> — Immediate harm." "<b>They flatter</b> — From the root of איש חלק, and all from the root חלק like חלק, because the parts are equal."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:27.612127867Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}